```ts
function stripExistingHeader(content: string): string {
	// Remove a leading copyright block comment.
	content = content.replace(/^\/\*\*?[\s\S]*?\*\/\s*/, '');
	// Remove a previously-generated DO NOT EDIT banner so re-syncing a file that
	// already carries the banner stays idempotent instead of stacking banners.
	content = content.replace(/^\/\/ allow-any-unicode-comment-file\n\/\/ DO NOT EDIT[^\n]*\n+/, '');
	return content;
}
```

**Rationale:** The script strips the source file's leading header, then prepends `COPYRIGHT` + `BANNER`. Previously it only stripped the leading block comment (copyright), not the two-line `// allow-any-unicode-comment-file` / `// DO NOT EDIT` banner. If a file that already carried the generated banner were ever fed back through `processFile`, the banner would be duplicated. Stripping it first makes the transformation idempotent — consistent with the `BANNER` constant and the AGENTS.md note that generated files carry a `DO NOT EDIT` banner. The regex is anchored and specific, so it only removes an existing generated banner and touches nothing else.

